# {{ title }}

The study timer keeps you focused and automatically logs every session. Sessions accumulate into a study heatmap in the dashboard, so you can see your consistency at a glance.

::toc{depth=2}

---

## Starting a session

Run **YAMD: Start Study Timer** from the command palette.

- A dropdown asks which course (if any notes have a `course:` front matter key).
  Pick one, or choose *(no course)* for an uncategorised session.
- The timer appears in the status bar at the bottom of the window, counting down
  from the configured session length (default 25 minutes).
- Click the status bar item to open the timer menu.

---

## The timer menu

Clicking the status bar item while a session is running shows:

| Option | What it does |
| ------ | ------------ |
| **Pause** | Freezes the countdown; time already elapsed is saved |
| **Resume** | Continues from where it was paused |
| **Finish and log** | Stops and logs the time you spent (minimum 1 minute) |
| **Cancel (no log)** | Stops without logging anything |

When no session is running, the menu offers to start one with the default
length, start for a specific course, or change the session duration.

---

## What gets logged

When a session finishes (or you choose **Finish and log**), YAMD:

1. Appends a record to `.yamd/study-log.json` at the workspace root.
2. If `yamd.study.logToDailyNote` is `true` (the default), appends a line to
   today's daily note under a **Study log** heading:

```text
- 14:05 · 25 min · CS201
```

The daily note is created if it doesn't exist yet, and the heading is added if
it isn't there.

---

## Daily note front matter

Every daily note created by YAMD (whether by the timer or by the **Open Today's
Daily Note** command) includes front matter:

```yamd
---
title: 2026-10-17
date: 2026-10-17
lang: en
---

# 2026-10-17

## Study log

- 09:00 · 25 min · CS201
- 14:05 · 50 min · MATH301
```

If you have a custom template set via `yamd.dailyNotes.template`, the template's
own front matter is used instead.

---

## Viewing the heatmap

Open the dashboard (**YAMD: Open Study Dashboard**). The heatmap shows the last
26 weeks, Monday to Sunday. Cell colour intensity reflects minutes studied:

| Shade | Minutes |
| ----- | ------- |
| Empty | 0 |
| Light | 1 – 29 |
| Medium | 30 – 59 |
| Dark | 60 – 119 |
| Darkest | 120+ |

The streak counter shows how many consecutive days you've had at least one
session.

---

## Settings

| Setting | Default | What it controls |
| ------- | ------- | ---------------- |
| `yamd.study.pomodoroMinutes` | `25` | Default session length |
| `yamd.study.logToDailyNote` | `true` | Append a line to today's daily note |

Change these in **Settings** → search *yamd study*.
